			"Message": "refactor(Cocoon): Normalize Effect-TS pipe-chain patterns\n\nStandardize three call sites in Output, Webview, and Factory modules to use `.pipe()` chaining instead of nesting effects inside runner functions.\n\n**Channel.ts:** Extract the `Channel` variable before wrapping in `Effect.succeed()`, replacing an inline cast pattern that collapsed declaration and return. Insert a TODO(EFX-30) marker for the planned `Effect.gen` → `async/await` migration.\n\n**Webview/Panel.ts:** Convert `Effect.runPromise(Logger.Debug(...))` to `Logger.Debug(...).pipe(Effect.runPromise)` — idiomatic left-to-right Effect-TS composition.\n\n**Factory.ts:** Replace `Effect.runFork(Ref.update(...))` (fire-and-forget fiber) with `void Ref.update(...).pipe(Effect.runPromise).catch(() => {})`, ensuring the ActivePanelsRef registry cleanup runs to completion rather than being scheduled on a fiber that may be abandoned. The explicit `void` + `.catch` matches Cocoon's established fire-and-forget idiom for side effects that must complete synchronously.\n\nNo behavioral changes to any module.",
			"SHA": "aa58914543fb46baadcd35fa8151c4510a76d30c"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T21:23:52Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				561,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Cocoon): Filter stale-channel frames in bidirectional gRPC stream\n\nMountain stamps Envelope.ChannelId (uint64, field 5) on every frame it pushes through the bidirectional streaming pump. When a stream is reopened — after a connection reset or re-registration — the old Mountain process may still send straggler frames through the previous registry entry before it shuts down.\n\nCapture the first nonzero ChannelId seen on each stream as the session identity. Frames arriving with a nonzero ChannelId that does not match the established session id are discarded immediately with a dev-log entry. ChannelId \"0\" (absent) is treated as a wildcard for backward compatibility with older Mountain builds and client-originated frames.\n\nAlso include the session ChannelId in the stream-closed dev-log for diagnostics.",
			"SHA": "661b375e7c7bd4a9cca703be91ec5d0980670a73"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T21:22:14Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				561,
				6
			],
			"Message": "feat(Cocoon): Implement willSave-as-REQUEST path; fix URI hydration and status bar paired colors\n\nAdd a `$willSaveDocument` REQUEST route in RequestRoutingHandler so Mountain can call Cocoon for TextEdits before persisting a document — the edits are returned in the response rather than fire-and-forget via `window.applyTextEdits`. Extract the listener collection logic from NotificationHandler into `CollectWillSaveDocumentEdits` with a 1.5s timeout cap on listener thenables; the notification path delegates to it and awaits before forwarding edits.\n\n**Bootstrap.ts:** Replace static stage-group arrays with a promise chain that links RPCServer → MountainConnection via `.then()`, letting the connect attempt start the moment the server settles instead of waiting for ModuleInterceptor too. Early-exit on RPCServer failure via `process.exit(1)` instead of `find`-based detection.\n\n**Env/Namespace.ts:** Hydrate every URI shape extensions hand to `openExternal` — string, real `vscode.Uri`, URI-like POJO, and the underscore-serialized wire form (`_scheme`, `_path`) — instead of casting with `String(Target)` which produces `[object Object]`. Implement `asExternalUri` that returns a real URI-compatible object with a `toString()` so extensions embedding the result in OAuth redirect URLs get a valid URL string. Respect Mountain's `isTelemetryEnabled` init payload when present.\n\n**Window/CreateStatusBarItem.ts:** Implement paired-theme-color semantics: when `statusBarItem.errorBackground` or `statusBarItem.warningBackground` is set, force the corresponding foreground (`errorForeground` / `warningForeground`) and serialize both as `{ id }` theme-color references instead of passing raw objects Mountain cannot resolve. Reject unsupported background theme IDs.\n\n**Window/Namespace.ts:** Extract `SendTreeRegister` with a retry that listens for `extensionHostInitialized` (plus a 2s fallback timer) so tree views registered before the Mountain connection is live still appear in the workbench. Fix `QuickPick.onDidChangeActive` vs `onDidChangeSelection` separation — each now has its own listener array, and assigning `items` resets the active item to the first entry and fires `onDidChangeActive` per VS Code semantics.",
			"SHA": "9445a0082898d69fe8ebab1f92c68974af1b73c4"
		},
